data.content:
## What Changed

Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi 10.0 upgrades to **Microsoft.OpenApi v2**, which has several breaking changes:

| .NET 9 (OpenApi v1) | .NET 10 (OpenApi v2) |
|---|---|
| `OpenApiString`, `OpenApiInteger`, etc. | `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode` |
| `schema.Example = new OpenApiString(...)` | `schema.Example = JsonNode.Parse("\"1.0\"")` |
| `schema.Nullable = true/false` | `schema.Type = JsonSchemaType.String \| JsonSchemaType.Null` |
| `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` inherits `Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>` | Has a `Schemes` dictionary property |
| `new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "..." }` | `new OpenApiReference("oauth2")` (type inferred from context) |

## Fixed Code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonNode.Parse("\"1.0\"");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference("oauth2")
    };
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new()
        {
            Schemes = new Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>
            {
                [oAuthScheme] = scopes
            }
        }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
            {
                // Remove Null from the type flags to mark as non-nullable
                property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type & ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
            }
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

### Summary of fixes:
1. **`OpenApiString` → `JsonNode.Parse(...)`** — all `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` types are gone.
2. **`Nullable` property removed** — nullability is now a flag on `schema.Type` (`JsonSchemaType.Null`).
3. **`OpenApiReference` simplified** — constructor takes the reference ID; type is inferred from usage context.
4. **`OpenApiSecurityRequirement`** — use the explicit `Schemes` property instead of dictionary-initializer syntax on the object itself.
